<title>USA: Dodge City feeder steers limited test - USDA.</title>
<headline>Dodge City feeder steers limited test - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DODGE CITY 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Feeder steers and heifers 300-600 lbs too few for a market test, limited test firm; 600-1000 lbs firm to $2.00 per cwt higher, compared with last week, USDA said.</p>
<p>Trade and demand good. Receipts 70 percent 600 lbs and over; 26 percent 600 lbs and under; 04 percent cows and bulls with 110 early.</p>
<p>Feeder Steers - (Figures in parentheses are weighted average prices) Medium and Large 1 - 600-650 lbs 84.00-88.00 (86.41); 10 head 684 lbs 82.50; 700-750 lbs 78.75-82.00 (80.71); 750-800 lbs 76.85-81.00 (79.66); 800-850 lbs 76.00-78.85 (77.62); 850-900 lbs 75.50-76.50 (75.73); 900-950 lbs 73.00-74.25 (73.38).</p>
<p>Feeder Heifers Medium and Large 1 - 600-650 lbs</p>
<p>74.75-79.75 (78.14); 650-700 lbs 75.50-80.00 (77.28); 700-750 lbs 74.00-76.75 (75.85); 750-800 lbs 74.00-76.10 (74.84); 16 head 817 lbs 76.25; 39 head 850 lbs 73.85. Medium and Large 1-2 500-550 lbs 78.00- 79.50 (78.88); 10 head 650 lbs 74.00; 700-750 lbs 72.00-73.75 (72.60); 750- 800 lbs 69.50-73.00 (71.20); 800-850 lbs 67.00-69.25 (68.89).</p>
<p>Receipts - 2,805   Last Week - 2,999   Last Year - 4,014</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
